Job Title: Software Developer Intern (5G). Company: Endava Việt Nam. Location: Quận Tân Bình. Seniority: Intern. Working Hours: FULL_TIME. Working Model: Onsite. Domains: IT Services and IT Consulting. Responsibilities: Company Description
Technology is our how. And people are our why.
By combining world-class engineering, industry expertise and a people-centric mindset, we consult and partner with our customers to create technological solutions that drive innovation and transform businesses.
From ideation to production, we support businesses with bespoke solutions across various industries, including payments, insurance, finance and banking, technology, media, telecommunications, retail and consumer goods, supply chain, healthcare and life sciences, automotive and travel.
Job Description
Development is the largest discipline at Endava. Our developers design, build, and release software products in multiple programming languages, frameworks, and libraries. Always collaborating with cross-functional project teams, our developers are adaptable problem-solvers with a client-oriented mindset.
As a 5G Radio Software Intern, you will have a chance to learn and practice with general technologies used in RADIO software such as C++, Autotools, Socket programming, Linux, Bash script, Git, Unit test, Automation test, GDB, Valgrind, …. Understanding overview about the system is also an important goal of this internship.
The project’s purpose is to design and develop a Radio Base Station (RBS) simulator.
RBS is a part of Radio Access Network in Mobile Network. RBS simulator is a simulation of an RBS which is a part of a Mobile Network in telecommunication system. It is the fixed transceiver that is the main communication point for wireless mobile client devices.
Agile/Scrum will be used during this project.. Required Qualifications: If you are studying or have just graduated from University with a Bachelor Degree in either Information Technology, Computer Science, Electronic and Telecommunication or a related degree with:
Strong IT background;
C/C++ software development passion;
High teamwork spirit;
Eager to learn new technologies;
Basic English communication;
Knowledge about embedded system, Realtime OS, Linux and Telecommunication is an advantage;. Skills: C++, Networking, Git, Linux, C language.

Job Title: Automation Test Engineer (Python, Embedded). Company: LG Electronics Development Vietnam (LGEDV). Location: Quận Tây Hồ. Seniority: Mid. Salary: 700.0-1400.0 USD. Working Hours: FULL_TIME. Working Model: Onsite. Domains: Software Products and Web Services. Responsibilities: As member of Automation Validation Team, you will be responsible for developing automation framework for testing Software Automotive domain as below:
Analyze software project requirements in Automotive (Telematics, AVN, Cluster);
Develop automation plug-ins, library for automation framework.
Create/update sample test scripts for testing.
Setup test environment; execute automation test scripts and ensure about automation test result reliability.
Log, verify & manage defects on defect tracking system
Follow function owner and leader assignments.
Escalate testing/developing risks and issues.. Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Electronics Engineering, Telecommunication Engineering or equivalent; etc;
Good at software programming, Python language and Robot Framework is preferred. If you have experience at performance / stability automation test and developing automation plug-in is plus;
Experienced working with embedded systems (hardware + software).
English: Basic conversational skills is required, intermediate preferred;
Good knowledge about Linux;
Has good logical thinking;
Had knowledge about RegEx is a plus.
Automotive (especially IVI: In Vehicle Infotainment) and ASPICE experience is a plus.
Understand embedded system is a plus.
Good at team working. Skills: Tester, Embedded, Agile, Python.

Job Title: Lead Java Engineer. Company: NAB Innovation Centre Vietnam. Location: Thành phố Thủ Đức. Seniority: Lead. Working Hours: FULL_TIME. Working Model: Onsite. Domains: Banking, IT Services and IT Consulting, Software Development Outsourcing, Software Products and Web Services, AI Software & Services. Responsibilities: ABOUT THE JOB
We are seeking motivated
Lead Java Engineer
who are passionate, results focused contributing to the transformation of NAB’s payment acceptance experience through innovation, digitisation, and integration. You will be part of our delivery team and will be responsible for providing technical leadership throughout all phases of the software delivery life cycle as we initiate a transformation of NAB technology.
At NAB, we believe success comes from our people. We're committed to supporting your talent and skills through your career, as you help us build a culture that affects change for our customers and for the community too.
MAIN RESPONSIBILITIES
Provide hands-on leadership to the design, development, and deployment of technical solutions;
Collaborate with other NAB's technology leaders towards improving and fulfilling the NAB technical direction;
Evangelizing and promoting Java /JavaScript - Node.js & React.js best practices;
Be passionate about Java /Node.js understanding how to implement advancement for existing or new systems;. Required Qualifications: 8 years' experienceas aTechnical Lead/Senior/Staff Engineer in a complex, enterprise-leveldevelopment environment; solid in architecting, developing, and deploying modernarchitectural patterns/techniques (microservices, DDD, TDD...)
Solid experience inJava 11+, Java open-source frameworks,including developing using modern frameworks, e.g.Spring Boot, Spring Cloud (less preferable)
Solid experience in designing & developingRESTful APIsandmicroservices-basedsystem
Solid experience withAWS / Azure Cloudservices is highly desired
Experience supporting a production service in aDevOps friendly environment
Solid experience inAgiledevelopment environments;
Well-versed in writing structured, well-documented, maintainable, and clean code;
Excellence in problem-solving and analytical skills;
Experience in leading and coaching at least one software engineering team on multiple projects;
Strong understanding of standard Software Engineering processes, Testing, and Agile methodology;. Skills: Java, Spring Boot, Microservices, Spring, AWS, English.

Job Title: Automotive Software Engineer (C++, OOP, Middleware). Company: LG Electronics Development Vietnam (LGEDV). Location: Quận Tây Hồ. Seniority: Mid. Salary: 800.0-2500.0 USD. Working Hours: FULL_TIME. Working Model: Onsite. Domains: IT Services and IT Consulting. Responsibilities: As member of Software Development team, you will be responsible for researching and developing applications for Car Infotainment, AVN (Audio Video Navigation) system, Cluster and, detailed as below:
Develop automotive products and technologies (included HMI Applications, HMI frameworks, Protocols to interface with HMI framework and middleware …);
Responsible for software delivery to head quarter;
Generate reports, communicate with local managements and head quarter.. Required Qualifications: Your skills and experience
** General requirements:
Bachelor degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Telecommunication Engineering, Mathematics, Mechanics and Informatics or equivalent.
Strong motivation to develop career in automotive software field.
Software development experience in C++ programming;
Having good knowledge with OOP, OOAD (Object-Oriented Analysis and Design);
Having hands-on experience to use JIRA, GIT and Gerrit;
Having hands-on experiences in developing large software systems;
** These skills would be considered as an advantage but not the must:
Experiences related to multi-thread, multi-process programming;. Skills: C++, Middleware, Linux, OOP, Embedded.

Job Title: Backend Engineer (Java, NodeJS, TypeScript) - Fintech. Company: Finhay. Location: Quận Ba Đình. Seniority: Mid. Salary: 1200.0-1800.0 USD. Working Hours: FULL_TIME. Working Model: Onsite. Domains: Financial Services. Responsibilities: Core Responsibilities
Thiết kế, phát triển và duy trì các backend services/API phục vụ các sản phẩm fintech, dữ liệu tài chính và nền tảng nội bộ của Finhay;
Xây dựng các RESTful API/GraphQL API có tính ổn định, bảo mật, dễ mở rộng và dễ tích hợp với các hệ thống khác;
Phát triển các business logic liên quan đến dữ liệu tài chính, tài khoản người dùng, giao dịch, báo cáo, tích hợp đối tác và các luồng nghiệp vụ nội bộ;
Tối ưu hiệu năng hệ thống, database query, caching, queue/job processing và khả năng chịu tải của backend services;
Tham gia thiết kế kiến trúc hệ thống, data model, luồng xử lý nghiệp vụ và giải pháp kỹ thuật cho các tính năng mới;
Phối hợp với Product Owner, QA, DevOps, Data và các team liên quan để phân tích yêu cầu, triển khai, debug và vận hành sản phẩm;
Đảm bảo chất lượng code thông qua unit test, integration test, code review, logging, monitoring và tài liệu kỹ thuật;
Maintain một số project nhỏ sử dụng Node.js khi cần, bao gồm fix bug, nâng cấp dependency, đọc hiểu source code và hỗ trợ vận hành.
System Integration & Data Products. Required Qualifications: Tối thiểu 2 năm kinh nghiệm phát triển backend bằng Java;
Thành thạo Java Core và có kinh nghiệm thực tế với Spring Boot/Spring Framework;
Có kinh nghiệm thiết kế và phát triển RESTful API, hiểu rõ HTTP methods, status codes, authentication, authorization, rate limiting, pagination;
Có kinh nghiệm làm việc với database quan hệ như PostgreSQL/MySQL/MariaDB; hiểu SQL, index, transaction, query optimization;
Có kiến thức về caching, message queue hoặc background jobs là lợi thế: Redis, Kafka, RabbitMQ, SQS hoặc tương đương;
Có kinh nghiệm viết unit test/integration test và quen thuộc với các công cụ như JUnit, Mockito, Testcontainers hoặc tương đương;
Quen thuộc với Git, CI/CD, Docker và quy trình phát triển phần mềm theo Agile/Scrum;
Có khả năng đọc hiểu, maintain và chỉnh sửa các project nhỏ bằng Node.js/JavaScript/TypeScript khi cần. Không yêu cầu là chuyên gia Node.js, nhưng cần sẵn sàng học và xử lý vấn đề ngoài Java stack.
Có kinh nghiệm xây dựng hệ thống fintech, securities, banking, payment, trading, market data hoặc các sản phẩm có yêu cầu cao về độ chính xác dữ liệu;
Hiểu biết về microservices, event-driven architecture, distributed system, observability, logging/metrics/tracing;. Skills: NodeJS, Spring, Java, AI, TypeScript.

Job Title: Automation Testing Software Engineer. Company: Datalogic Việt Nam. Location: Thành phố Thủ Đức. Seniority: Mid. Working Hours: FULL_TIME. Working Model: Onsite. Domains: Software Products and Web Services. Responsibilities: Datalogic is currently hiring Automation Testing Engineers across Junior, Middle, Senior, and Lead levels to support the development of our products.
Role Main activities
Draw sketches of product ideas and design mockups of proposed products;
Contribute to define detailed project requirements and specifications;
Define the action plan within the product development in terms of the needed time/resources;
Develop the assigned parts of the project, paying attention to the guidelines provided by the team leaders
Contribute to the validation-test plans, perform measurements and functional tests on prototypes, assuring full coverage of all requirements;
Ensure design files and technical documentation are kept up to date and stored in accordance with departmental procedures;
Embrace innovation culture of our Company, contributing to generate invention disclosures and to scout/evaluate novel and differentiating technologies;
Participate in the maintenance of existing products, with the aim also to solve problems arisen from field or production.. Required Qualifications: Experience in software testing, with a focus on automatic identification products.
Experience in test automation frameworks and related tool such as: Python, Java, TypeScript, API testing, Selenium, Appium, Playwright, Test Complete, etc.
Experience about electronics and programming tools
Proficient in test management tools such as Jira, JAZZ IBM, and experience with other Agile project management tools.
Experience of Linux, Git, JFrog and Jenkins
Strong analytical and problem-solving skills: Ability to identify and troubleshoot complex technical issues.
Experience leveraging AI-assisted tools (e.g., ChatGPT, GitHub Copilot, Cursor, Claude) to generate test cases, automate test scripts, analyze test results, and improve testing efficiency
Understanding of cloud platforms (e.g., AWS, Azure, Google Cloud) and cloud application (nice to have)
Language: English (good command in both speaking & listening)
Ability to effectively prioritize tasks and meet deadlines.. Skills: Tester, API, Automation Test, Selenium, Java.

